Terraform: Secret Creation. You want to:
terraform {
  required_providers {
    local = {
      source  = "hashicorp/local"
      version = "2.1.0"
    }
  }
}

provider "local" {}

variable "secret" {
  type      = string
  sensitive = true
}

resource "local_file" "secret" {
  filename        = "/run/secret"
  content         = var.secret
  file_permission = "0600"
}
The `secret` variable has no default, so Terraform expects it supplied externally - via `TF_VAR_secret=<value> terraform apply`, which is the standard way to pass a variable through an environment variable rather than a `.tfvars` file, keeping it out of any committed file. `file_permission = "0600"` sets the created file's mode explicitly so it's readable/writable only by its owner, appropriate for a file holding secret content, and marking the variable `sensitive = true` keeps its value redacted from Terraform's CLI plan/apply output.
